    "content": "## Test Summary - Job Board Application Validation\n\n**Test Results: 17 PASS, 2 FAIL (89.5% completion)**\n\n### ✅ Passing Tests (17):\n\n**Functionality:**\n- **FT-1**: Employers can publish jobs with all required fields (title, industry, employment type, location, salary, description, skills). Job appears in both employer dashboard and job seeker listing.\n- **FT-2**: Employers can delete jobs with confirmation dialog. Deletion removes job and all associated applications from all views.\n- **FT-3**: Employer dashboard displays accurate active job counts and total application counts that update correctly.\n- **FT-4**: Employer dashboard allows opening each job's application list to view all applications.\n- **FT-5**: Job seekers can browse complete job listings and view full job details on detail pages.\n- **FT-6**: Job seekers can filter by industry, location, and employment type individually or in combination. Clearing restores full list.\n- **FT-7**: Keyword search matches job titles, company names, and required skills with case-insensitive matching. Results update immediately.\n- **FT-8**: Job seekers can submit applications with name, email, optional phone, and message, receiving clear success confirmation.\n\n**Constraints:**\n- **CS-9**: Application form validation prevents submission without required fields (name, email, message) and validates email syntax.\n- **CS-10**: Job posting form validation prevents submission without all required fields (title, industry, type, location, description, salary, at least one skill).\n\n**Interaction:**\n- **IX-13**: Successfully submitted applications appear in employer dashboard with all submitted information.\n- **IX-14**: Search and filter criteria immediately refresh matching jobs and result counts.\n- **IX-19**: Published jobs, submitted applications, and deletions persist after page reload.\n\n**Content:**\n- **CT-15**: Job cards display title, company, industry, employment type, location, salary range, posting date, and required skills.\n- **CT-16**: Job details page displays all information matching the selected listing.\n- **CT-17**: Employer can view applicant name, email, phone, message, and submission date for each application.\n- **CT-20**: Newly published jobs and applications display accurate submission dates relative to current date.\n\n### ❌ Failing Tests (2):\n\n**Functionality:**\n- **FT-18**: FAIL - No edit functionality found for published jobs. The employer dashboard only provides a delete option; no edit button or capability exists to modify job details after publication.\n\n**Constraints:**\n- **CS-11**: FAIL - System accepts duplicate email applications for the same job from different applicants. Both applications are stored and displayed. The system should prevent subsequent applications from the same email for the same job.\n\n### Key Findings:\nThe application successfully implements core job board functionality including job posting, browsing, filtering, searching, and application management with good data persistence. However, two important features are missing: the ability to edit published jobs and duplicate application prevention by email."
